{
  "Someone’s picture, or their initials, or a person icon, with their presence on its corner. A group stacks or spreads them and counts the ones it does not show.": "",
  "Picture, initials, icon": "",
  "The picture shows once it has loaded; until then, and when it cannot load, the initials show. Without a name the person icon does.": "",
  "Tones and shapes": "",
  "Sizes and presence": "",
  "`max` shows that many and counts the rest in a `+N`; `total` counts those not given as well. The group sets the size of all its avatars.": "",
  "With a name or a label the avatar is an image with that name (`role=\"img\"`); the presence is said after it (“Ada Lovelace, Away”).": "",
  "An avatar with nothing to say (no name, no label, no presence) is hidden from screen readers.": "",
  "The picture has an empty `alt`: the avatar itself carries the name.": "",
  "`role=\"group\"` with its label; the `+N` says how many are not shown (“8 more people”).": "",
  "The presence is not said by colour alone: it is in the name screen readers hear, and Fluent draws a mark in the dot.": "",
  "Initials are written in the capitals of the kit language (`uiLocale`): “ilgin” is “İ” in Turkish. The presence and the `+N` texts are kit texts (`presenceOnline` … `presenceOffline`, `avatarPresence`, `moreItems`, `avatarGroupMore`) and change with it.": "",
  "The avatar. `data-size`, `data-shape`, `data-tone`.": "",
  "The picture. `data-pending` until it loads.": "",
  "The initials, and the person icon shown without them.": "",
  "The presence dot. `data-status`.": "",
  "The group. `data-size`, `data-layout`; an avatar it does not show has `data-beyond`.": "",
  "The `+N` avatar.": "",
  "Unit: the avatar at rest (the standard tone) and in each tone.": "",
  "Units: the person icon; the presence dot (its ring, per presence); a mark inside the dot, per presence.": "",
  "The avatar, its initials, its icon, its dot and its square corners, per size.": "",
  "The tone and shape an avatar takes when none is given.": "",
  "Unit: the ring that parts a stacked avatar from the one it covers.": "",
  "How far stacked avatars go under each other, the space between spread ones, and the layout taken when none is given.": "",
  "Avatar props": "",
  "The picture. Until it loads, or when it cannot, the initials (else the person icon) show.": "",
  "Whose avatar it is: the initials are made from it, and screen readers say it.": "",
  "Initials of your own instead of the ones made from `name`.": "",
  "What screen readers say instead of the name.": "",
  "`xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`. In a group, the group’s.": "",
  "the language’s (`circle`)": "",
  "`circle`, `square` (with the language’s corners for its size).": "",
  "`standard`, `accent`, `info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`, or `auto`: one taken from the name, the same for the same name everywhere. Material and Lilac take `accent`, the others `standard`.": "",
  "`online`, `away`, `busy`, `offline`: a presence dot on the lower end corner.": "",
  "Avatar properties": "",
  "The initials it shows: the ones given, else the ones made from the name.": "",
  "Whether the picture is what shows now (it loaded).": "",
  "AvatarGroup props": "",
  "The size of every avatar in it.": "",
  "the language’s (`stack`)": "",
  "`stack`: each over the one before it; `spread`: side by side.": "",
  "The most avatars shown; the others are counted in a `+N` after them.": "",
  "How many there are in all, when only some are given; the rest are counted in the `+N`.": "",
  "What screen readers call the group (“Members”).": "",
  "AvatarGroup properties": "",
  "The elements of the avatars given, in order, from JSX lists too (the `+N` is not one of them).": "",
  "How many are counted in the `+N`; 0 when it does not show.": "",
  "The initials an avatar makes of a name: the first letters of its first and last words, in the capitals of the language.": ""
